@@ -32,3 +32,17 @@ Tests run with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs the TypeScript tests directly
   child); a plain `Error` when a `test` finds a different value.
 - `test` compares values by JSON equality (member order is irrelevant, `1` is not `"1"`).
 - Paths use `resolvePointer`'s rules; `__proto__` and `constructor` are ordinary member names.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a merge patch to `target` and
+returns the merged document.
+
+- A patch that is not an object (including an array or `null`) replaces the target. An object patch
+  is merged member by member: `null` deletes the member, any other value is merged recursively, and a
+  non-object target is treated as `{}`.
+- Arrays are replaced as a whole, so `null` inside an array is kept. Because `null` means "delete", a
+  merge patch cannot set a member to `null`.
+- The inputs are never mutated and the result shares no structure with them.
+- `TypeError` when `patch` is not a JSON value (`undefined`, functions, `NaN`/`Infinity`, sparse
+  array holes...). `__proto__` and `constructor` are ordinary member names.
